---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Peptide OEM & Private Label for Brands — Packaging, Labels, Documentation" description="OEM and private-label research peptide supply for brands: custom labels, boxes, batch coding, documentation packages and compliance-reviewed artwork." canonical="/applications/oem-brands/">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Applications › OEM brands</p>
    <h1>OEM and private label for brands</h1>
    <div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer.</strong> A private-label peptide program is a documentation and labelling project before it is a manufacturing project. The label, the batch code and the COA must agree, and the claims must survive the destination market's rules.</div>
    <p class="lead muted">We work with brands that need a supplier able to produce, label, pack and document under their identity — without inventing claims the product cannot support.</p>

    <h2>What can be customized</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Options</th><th>Minimum</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Vial label</td><td>Brand, SKU, strength, batch, RUO statement, QR to COA</td><td>500 labels per SKU</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Box / carton</td><td>Printed box, insert card, security seal</td><td>500 units</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Documentation</td><td>Branded COA template, MSDS, storage card</td><td>With first order</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Vial format</td><td>2/3/5/10 mL amber or clear, crimp or flip-off</td><td>By SKU</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Batch coding</td><td>Your convention or ours</td><td>By agreement</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>The label rules we will not bend</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No therapeutic, dosing or human-use claims.</li>
      <li>"For laboratory research use only" on label and box.</li>
      <li>No fake certification marks or unverifiable standards.</li>
      <li>Batch number and expiry printed, not implied.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Process</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Brief: products, strengths, volumes, target markets.</li>
      <li>Compliance review of label claims and destination requirements.</li>
      <li>Artwork proof and sample approval.</li>
      <li>Production, fill, label, pack, QC release.</li>
      <li>Documentation pack and shipment.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>See the full <a href="/oem-private-label/">OEM / private label page</a> and the <a href="/knowledge/china-peptide-sourcing-framework/">sourcing framework</a>.</p>

    <p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Discuss an OEM project</a> <a class="wa-btn" href={site.whatsappLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="margin-left:10px;">💬 WhatsApp</a></p>
    <div class="ruo">{site.ruo}</div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
